---
import DocPage from '../layouts/DocPage.astro';
import { GITHUB_URL, WIKI_URL } from '../consts';
---

<DocPage
	eyebrow="FAQ"
	title="Questions"
	description="Common questions about the HippOS beta. Can't find an answer? Ask in the Discord."
>
	<h2>Is HippOS free?</h2>
	<p>Yes. HippOS is open source under the GPLv3. The source is on <a href={GITHUB_URL}>GitHub</a>.</p>

	<h2>Why do I need Discord to download it?</h2>
	<p>
		HippOS is in beta, and the Discord is where bug reports, fixes and release announcements happen. Tying downloads
		to it means everyone running a beta can be reached when something breaks.
	</p>

	<h2>Does it come with games or BIOS files?</h2>
	<p>
		No. HippOS comes with emulators and a few free games and ports from the built-in content store. You supply your
		own game dumps and BIOS files.
	</p>

	<h2>Will an update wipe my games or saves?</h2>
	<p>
		No. The OS and your data live separately. Updates replace the OS and leave <code>/userdata</code> alone, including
		ROMs, saves, BIOS, screenshots and settings. If an update goes wrong, HippOS can roll back to the previous version.
	</p>

	<h2>How do I get to a desktop?</h2>
	<p>
		Press <strong>F1</strong> in EmulationStation (or the device's mode button on supported handhelds). Log out to
		return to EmulationStation. LXQt is the default desktop. You can pick a different one from
		<strong>Main Menu → Select Desktop</strong>.
	</p>

	<h2>Can I play PC games?</h2>
	<p>
		Yes. Steam is built in and your installed Steam games appear in EmulationStation. Wine and Lutris handle other
		Windows games, and Bazaar gives you the full Flathub catalogue for apps like Heroic and Bottles.
	</p>

	<h2>Can I run Android apps?</h2>
	<p>Yes. Waydroid runs Android apps, and they appear in EmulationStation next to your emulators.</p>

	<h2>Can I dual-boot?</h2>
	<p>
		Yes. The installer can put HippOS into free space or an existing partition next to another OS. See <a href="/install">Install</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>Something broke. How do I report it?</h2>
	<p>
		Open <strong>Main Menu → Upload Logs</strong>, then post in the Discord beta channel with your device model and what you
		were doing. Logs include the previous boot, so they're still useful after a crash and reboot.
	</p>

	<h2>Where's the documentation?</h2>
	<p>Guides and per-system notes live on the <a href={WIKI_URL}>HippOS wiki</a>.</p>
</DocPage>
